{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add an `mcp` autodeploy target to `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` implementing the ADR 0079\namendment's blue-green pointer-swap, so on-box `rebar-mcp` tracks `origin/main` without killing\nan in-flight certified op (eliminates bug 7b4a). Scope: MCP deploy path only (edge = esok,\nsecrets = avians); no new timer (existing `rebar-autodeploy.timer`→`.service`).\n\n## Approach (blue-green, ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur / 0079)\nModel on the LOCAL `origin/main` updater (`sticky-genetic-narwhal`): immutable release + atomic\npointer swap + retire-when-idle, NOT stop-and-drain. On an MCP source change:\n1. Build + tag immutable `compose-mcp:<target-sha>` (`docker compose build mcp`).\n2. **Memory pre-check BEFORE the 2x overlap** (t4g.large 8 GiB): `MemAvailable` (`/proc/meminfo`,\n   MB) `< MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` (default 1024) ABORTS — `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT`, backoff, NO second\n   container. Unreadable fails OPEN; `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB` overrides.\n3. Start a NEW container alongside old via **`docker run -d`** on a FREE A/B host port (see Run\n   mechanism); one-in/one-out, never N.\n4. Health-check the NEW `/health` 200 within `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT` (default 120). On failure:\n   `docker rm -f` new, leave OLD include UNCHANGED, `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` `mcp-unhealthy`, backoff,\n   exit 1.\n5. **Atomically flip the nginx `/mcp/` upstream**: back up the include, write\n   `server 127.0.0.1:<newport>;` to a dotfile temp NOT matching the `mcp-upstream*.conf` glob,\n   `mv` (atomic rename) over `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`, `nginx -t`, `nginx -s reload`. On\n   failure: RESTORE backup, `docker rm -f` new, backoff, exit 1. DONE at a successful reload;\n   never waited on/killed an op.\n6. **Retire the OLD container off the critical path**, gated by a \"still serving?\" check on its\n   `/health` `in_flight` gauge. Retain newest `MCP_RELEASES_KEEP` (default 1); remove older ones\n   ONLY when idle; NEVER kill `in_flight>0`. If the managed count exceeds `MCP_RELEASES_CAP`\n   (default 3) because busy containers can't be reclaimed, emit `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP`\n   instead of killing a live one (also the port-exhaustion guard — see Run mechanism). Since\n   `autodeploy.sh` exits early when up-to-date, also run `mcp_retire_sweep` on the no-op tick\n   (like `reclaim_under_pressure`) so retirement re-triggers once an old container goes idle.\n\n## Run mechanism + the original compose container (bootstrap)\n`docker compose up mcp` pins `8091` and would collide, so the NEW container starts via\n**`docker run -d`** from `compose-mcp:<sha>` (helper `mcp_run_new`) on a FREE blue-green HOST\nport `-p 127.0.0.1:<newport>:8091` (container port stays 8091): `newport` = whichever of\n`MCP_PORT_A=8092`/`MCP_PORT_B=8093` is NOT currently bound by a managed container (8091 is\nRESERVED for the compose-original). If BOTH A and B are bound by un-reclaimable (in_flight>0)\ncontainers, the deploy does NOT start a colliding 3rd — it emits `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` +\nbackoff and starts nothing. So managed ports are EXACTLY {8091,8092,8093} = `MCP_RELEASES_CAP=3`\n(cap and port pool coincide). Flags reproduce the compose `mcp:` service EXACTLY — `--env-file\n.env`, every `REBAR_MCP_*`/`REBAR_OPCERT_*` var with compose's literal `${VAR:-default}` values\n(`docker run` does NOT interpolate), the two `:ro` secret mounts, `--restart always`,\n`--stop-timeout 1260` — the compose-parity oracle pins the set.\n\nAt boot `compose-up.sh` `docker compose up -d`s the whole stack: the ORIGINAL backend is\n`compose-mcp-1` on 8091 (seed include→8091). The managed MCP set (sweep/cap count over) = names\nmatching `MCP_CONTAINER_PREFIX` (`rebar-mcp`) OR `MCP_COMPOSE_CONTAINER` (`compose-mcp-1`), so\nthat first OLD backend is adopted into retire-when-idle by the same liveness gate (autodeploy\nnever `docker compose up mcp`); reboot re-creates it on 8091 with no collision. Sweep discovers\neach old port via `docker port <name> 8091/tcp`; an unreadable OLD `/health` read = still-serving\n(fail-safe).\n\n## Change detection + blast radius\n`MCP_PATHS='src/rebar infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp infra/compose/docker-compose.yml uv.lock pyproject.toml'`\n— esok's canonical `mcp:` compose-comment set. Diffed `deployed..target` it triggers ONLY `mcp`;\n`src/rebar`+`docker-compose.yml` are shared with `BOT_PATHS`, so a shared change triggers BOTH\ntargets in independent `if changed` blocks. `gerrit` untouched (before/after gerrit-id assert).\n`flock` still serializes.\n\n## Failure interaction with deployed-sha + backoff\nThe `mcp` branch failure is FATAL like `review-bot` (`record_backoff_failure` + `exit 1`), so\n`deployed-sha` is not advanced and the deploy retries next tick. For a shared change, review-bot\nruns first and its idempotent rebuild simply repeats until mcp also succeeds.\n\n## Alerting (marker → observability → CloudWatch → SNS; NO direct SNS publish)\nautodeploy.sh has no `sns:Publish` path and must not gain one. Like every existing autodeploy\nalert: a countable `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_* {json}` → `observability.sh`\n`publish_autodeploy_marker_delta` greps the journal into a dimensionless `rebar/host` metric → a\nterraform `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` → `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`. Adds tokens\n`AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` + `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` (distinct from `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`); two\nmarker-delta calls (+ offset files) → `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort`;\ntwo alarms mirroring `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`'s 900s/2-of-4/Sum>0/notBreaching shape.\n\n## Portability (`project.portability`)\nTrigger is the on-box systemd/launchd timer polling the git mirror — operation-linked, not CI;\nflip/retire run in-process. Works with any/no CI provider.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real subprocess/bash integration, temp git repos + fake docker/nginx**. Tests stub\n  the box binaries onto PATH and run the REAL `autodeploy.sh`, in `tests/scripts/`. Oracles:\n  - Change detection (REAL temp git repo, two commits, asserted via the docker call log): an\n    MCP-only change (touch `Dockerfile.mcp`) triggers `mcp` and NO review-bot/gerrit rebuild; a\n    review-bot-only change (`Dockerfile.reviewbot`) does the inverse; a shared `src/rebar` change\n    triggers BOTH independently.\n  - Cutover order start-new → health → flip → retire (recorded docker/nginx/curl log); returns\n    success WITHOUT waiting on `in_flight` (with `in_flight>0` on OLD it still flips and exits 0).\n  - Retire honors liveness: an OLD `in_flight>0` container is NOT killed (no `docker rm` of it);\n    over `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` the `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` marker is emitted, no live container\n    deleted.\n  - Port exhaustion: with BOTH A and B bound by `in_flight>0` containers, a new MCP change does\n    NOT `docker run -p` on an occupied port (no 3rd container); `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP`\n    emitted, backoff recorded.\n  - Memory pre-check: `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB < MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` ABORTS — no second container started,\n    `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` emitted, backoff recorded, include unchanged.\n  - Health-check OR nginx reload failure leaves the OLD include byte-identical\n    (`AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`, backoff, `deployed-sha` not advanced); a retry next healthy tick flips it.\n  - `gerrit` container id UNCHANGED across an mcp deploy (blast radius).\n  - Compose parity: a test parses the `mcp:` service in `docker-compose.yml` and asserts\n    `mcp_run_new`'s `docker run` env keys+values and `:ro` mounts match it — a drift guard,\n    since `/health` is auth-independent (mounted outside auth middleware) and cannot catch a\n    wrong `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_*`/`ALLOWED_HOSTS`.\n- [ ] observability.sh publishes `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort`; two\n  terraform CloudWatch alarms route them to `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn` (mirror\n  `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`'s shape).\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive (new `if changed \"$MCP_PATHS\"` block + no-op sweep); other targets unchanged (existing\nautodeploy tests stay green); ADRs 0079/0104 document it. Rollback = revert the additions AND\nreset the include to `server 127.0.0.1:8091;` (edge points back at compose-managed 8091).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur, cibophobic-holohedral-esok."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787628587165142001,"uuid":"64a825ab-6b2f-4181-b451-86bf8addad7e"}